      "ordinal": 8,
      "duty": "adversarial-review",
      "model": "gpt-5.6-sol",
      "requests": 11,
      "costUsd": 0.2900592,
      "precededBy": {
       "kind": "handoff",
       "seq": 904,
       "duty": "implement",
       "status": "complete",
       "next": "adversarial-review",
       "why": "This is the second review cycle for this specific finding; a final check confirms the fix is correct and no new issues were introduced before marking the card done.",
       "summary": "Fixed the overdue-date timezone bug flagged by adversarial review, and added regression coverage.\n\n- Extracted the date logic from `public/app.js` into a new `public/dateUtils.js` module exporting `todayISO(date)` and `isOverdue(todo, date)`, both accepting an injectable `Date` (defaulting to `new Date()`) so they're unit-testable outside a browser.\n- `todayISO` now builds `YYYY-MM-DD` from `getFullYear()`/`getMonth()`/`getDate()` (local calendar date) instead of `new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)` (UTC date), fixing the local-midnight boundary bug.\n- `app.js` now imports `isOverdue` from `dateUtils.js` (loaded as an ES module via `<script type=\"module\">`, already the case in `index.html`).\n- Added `test/dateUtils.test.js` (4 tests) covering the exact boundary from the review finding: with `TZ=Europe/Lisbon`, a local time of 2026-08-30 00:30 is 2026-08-29 23:30 UTC — the test asserts"
      }
     }
